# ET-8 generated task sets. The old rule excluded task_*.json as "regenerable: et8_env.py gen" --
# but NO SEED WAS EVER RECORDED, so v0 and v1 are not regenerable, and v0's files were never
# committed at all: its localisation numbers are permanently unauditable. The whole set is 7.8 MB
# and 0.2 MB gzipped, which was never the reason to exclude it. Ri's ruling after the v1 defect:
# every run persists the artifacts a later question could need, or its downstream claims are
# marked unauditable. So the task sets are TRACKED.
# experience/tasks/*/task_*.json
# experience/traj/  -- TRACKED, same ruling as the task sets. These are the trajectories every
# downstream claim reads: the A/C/F comparisons, the steering vectors, the probe, the G-trivial
# decomposition. et6's chess self-play games were kept only in memory and are GONE, which is why
# P8's adapter had nothing to confirm; v0's task files were never committed and its numbers are
# permanently unauditable. 26 MB total. Persist what a later question needs, or mark the claim.
